Bugfix: Correctly apply a `--tag` filter that contains an empty tag

The empty tag in a `--tag` or `--keep-tag` list selects snapshots without
any tags. Restic stopped looking at a tag list once it reached the empty
tag, so a list like `,foo` matched every untagged snapshot instead of
matching nothing, while the equivalent `foo,` matched nothing. For
`forget` that meant snapshots outside the filter were considered for
removal.

Restic now requires an empty tag to be the only tag in its list. A list
that combines it with another tag, such as `,foo` or `foo,`, is rejected
when the command line is parsed, instead of quietly selecting either the
wrong snapshots or none at all.

